# Benchmarks

What pg_stat_statement_context costs on top of `pg_stat_statements` alone, measured with pgbench. This page is **generated**: `bench/analyze.py doc` fills in the results from the raw data committed under [`bench/results/`](../bench/results/), and the prose comes from [`bench/benchmarks.md.in`](../bench/benchmarks.md.in). How to run the suite, and how to run it on dedicated hardware, is in [`bench/README.md`](../bench/README.md).

**Read this first.** The only campaign so far ran in a **Docker Desktop VM on a laptop (Apple M1 Max, macOS)**. That is not production hardware: the VM's vCPUs float across performance and efficiency cores, and the host's scheduler, power management and other processes add noise that nothing inside the VM can see. Treat the results as relative costs on that machine, read their confidence intervals, and don't quote the absolute TPS or latency. Dedicated Linux x86 and Graviton runs are left to the maintainers ([instructions](../bench/README.md#dedicated-hardware)); their results will appear here when they are committed.

